00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:52.219
- Okay. so. um...
- Can I ask you something now?

226
00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:54.297
- JOSH: Yeah.
- ASHLEY: Can I give you some advice?

227
00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.099
- JOSH: Umm. sure. Yeah.
- ASHLEY: This is an interview. right?

228
00:11:57.175 --> 00:11:59.223
- JOSH: Yeah.
- ASHLEY: So maybe you should ask me

229
00:11:59.302 --> 00:12:00.849
some open-ended questions.

230
00:12:00.929 --> 00:12:03.603
You know. like. things that don't
just warrant yes or no answers.

231
00:12:03.681 --> 00:12:05.183
Just. like. get me to talk...

232
00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:06.813
JOSH:
Okay. yeah. No. Sure.

233
00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:09.354
Is this the same place?

234
00:12:11.773 --> 00:12:16.370
WOMAN: She just had
this charm about her that was electric.

235
00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:21.161
I think because of that
she could get a lot out of people.

236
00:12:21.241 --> 00:12:23.790
people trusted her.
saw her as a confidant.

237
00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:27.873
Jack was kind of pushing
the lawyer thing.

238
00:12:27.956 --> 00:12:31.631
but truly I... I think
Ashley's passion was journalism.

239
00:12:35.213 --> 00:12:37.149
<i>ASHLEY (on TV):
Good morning. Canyon Park High School.</i>

240
00:12:37.173 --> 00:12:39.346
<i>I'm Ashley Foster. CPTV.</i>

241
00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:43.280
Just want to say hello to all the new
freshmen in the building.

242
00:12:43.304 --> 00:12:44.521
Welcome aboard.

243
00:12:45.765 --> 00:12:47.733
I know locker combinations
can be tricky.

244
00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:49.903
but you'll make it through
just like I did.

245
00:12:49.978 --> 00:12:51.730
So just keep trying.

246
00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:53.065
Together. we're a team...

247
00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:56.238
and this is not teamwork.

248
00:12:56.317 --> 00:12:58.661
- (chuckles) That's cute.
- MELISSA: Yeah.

249
00:12:58.736 --> 00:13:00.296
SOPHIE:
What did you guys think of Josh?

250
00:13:00.905 --> 00:13:01.997
We didn't know him.

251
00:13:04.659 --> 00:13:07.208
- MELISSA: Is that Josh's yearbook?
- SOPHIE: Yeah. umm...

252
00:13:07.704 --> 00:13:08.796
Ashley signed it.

253
00:13:08.871 --> 00:13:10.140
- MELISSA: Oh really?
- SOPHIE: Yeah.

254
00:13:10.164 --> 00:13:11.962
- There it is.
- MELISSA: Oh!

255
00:13:12.041 --> 00:13:13.918
Look at that.
(chuckles)

256
00:13:15.837 --> 00:13:18.886
I mean. he was never one of these kids
that came over to the house.

257
00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:23.391
That's it. Josh Bishop.

258
00:13:24.887 --> 00:13:26.991
- Seems like she had a lot of friends.
- Oh. she did. yeah.

259
00:13:27.015 --> 00:13:28.858
She was a charmer.

260
00:13:28.933 --> 00:13:32.028
Have you ever... Have you ever heard
the story of Ezekiel's wheel?

261
00:13:33.021 --> 00:13:34.113
JOSH: Umm...

262
00:13:35.732 --> 00:13:39.362
- It-It's from the Bible.
- JOSH: Oh. Yeah. Definitely not.

263
00:13:39.444 --> 00:13:42.994
Ezekiel describes God
coming down from heaven in a chariot.

264
00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:46.201
It's lighting up the sky.
but all along the outside are eyes.

265
00:13:48.286 --> 00:13:49.726
JOSH:
Why would God need a spaceship?

266
00:13:49.787 --> 00:13:52.336
(laughing)
Exactly.

267
00:13:52.415 --> 00:13:54.008
because he is space.

268
00:13:56.002 --> 00:13:57.299
Yeah.

269
00:13:57.378 --> 00:13:59.231
- JOSH: All right. we're done. It's cool.
- It's done?

270
00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:01.553
- JOSH: Yeah. yeah. yeah.
- Great. Okay. Bye.

271
00:14:01.632 --> 00:14:02.849
JOSH:
Thanks for doing it.

272
00:14:08.848 --> 00:14:12.648
CAROLINE: <i>A very sweet girl.
I met her</i> a <i>few times.</i>

273
00:14:12.727 --> 00:14:15.480
I definitely know that
Josh had a crush on her and...

274
00:14:17.148 --> 00:14:18.195
I'm hoping...

275
00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:21.911
Now I'm going to cry.
I'm hoping she liked him.

276
00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:24.660
Just because they...

277
00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:29.085
spent so much time together.
it would have been nice to know that he.

278
00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.788
in his short life.
could experience that.

279
00:14:36.667 --> 00:14:38.645
- SOPHIE: That's Ashley's handwriting.
- CAROLINE: Mm-hmm.

280
00:14:38.669 --> 00:14:40.262
<i>SOPHIE: And how much
do you know about</i>

281
00:14:40.338 --> 00:14:42.887
what Ashley and Josh
were working on?

282
00:14:42.965 --> 00:14:46.060
We certainly didn't know
any of that until...

283
00:14:46.135 --> 00:14:47.261
- later.
- Later.

284
00:14:47.345 --> 00:14:49.643
- It was after.
- Yeah. Yeah.

285
00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.599
- We knew very little.
- Mm-hmm.

286
00:14:53.726 --> 00:14:55.194
(player whirring)

287
00:15:00.608 --> 00:15:02.986
We're going to meet
with some astronomers.

288
00:15:03.069 --> 00:15:04.713
- JOSH: Okay.
- They're going to have rocks

289
00:15:04.737 --> 00:15:06.910
and all different kinds
of stuff to show us.

290
00:15:06.989 --> 00:15:10.189
so we've got to be prepared. and we need
to make sure that we're on our "A" game.

291
00:15:10.451 --> 00:15:12.124
JOSH:
What does our "A" game mean?

292
00:15:12.203 --> 00:15:14.331
We just have to be professional.

293
00:15:14.414 --> 00:15:18.635
But I'm feeling... I feel like I've been
pretty professional so far. thank you.

294
00:15:18.709 --> 00:15:21.007
I don't think
I'm exactly amateur hour.

295
00:15:21.087 --> 00:15:23.260
I know. but I-I guess
I'm just a little nervous.

296
00:15:23.339 --> 00:15:24.511
I want everything to go good.

297
00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.558
Well. do you have
any questions prepared?

298
00:15:26.634 --> 00:15:29.321
I have a ton. they're in my backpack.
Do you have my backpack by the way?

299
00:15:29.345 --> 00:15:30.767
JOSH:
Yeah. I do.

300
00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:39.317
MAN: Have you ever held
a meteorite before?

301
00:15:40.356 --> 00:15:41.824
I'll start with this one.

302
00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:45.570
ASHLEY:
Whoa! (laughing)

303
00:15:45.653 --> 00:15:49.874
MAN: We get phone calls about UFOs
kind of frequently.

304
00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:53.203
JOSH: So when the Phoenix Lights happened.
were people calling and asking?

305
00:15:53.286 --> 00:15:55.914
Uh... yeah. they were.

306
00:15:55.997 --> 00:15:57.670
- A few.
- ASHLEY: He shot the footage.

307
00:15:57.748 --> 00:16:00.627
- Oh. you shot the footage?
- (laughing) That's right. yeah.

308
00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:03.805
Oh. congratulations!
Can you learn to focus?

309
00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.507
- (both laughing)
- There you go.

310
00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.638
STEVE <i>(on</i> TV): <i>They're in</i>
a <i>formation of some kind.</i>

311
00:16:07.717 --> 00:16:09.139
<i>but they're not really moving.</i>

312
00:16:09.218 --> 00:16:11.266
Okay. that's more likely flares.

313
00:16:11.345 --> 00:16:13.814
(radio chatter)

314
00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.814
<i>DUN: The flares are probably
fifty to a hundred miles away.</i>

315
00:16:16.893 --> 00:16:20.147
<i>So you don't see the smoke. You just see
a bright light that just hangs there</i>

316
00:16:20.229 --> 00:16:22.607
<i>because of the parachute
to hold them in place.</i>

317
00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.793
ASHLEY: Would you say you're
a hundred percent sure it's not

318
00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:27.912
or you're ninety-nine percent sure
and still open to the possibility?

319
00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:32.117
No. I'm a hundred percent sure
that-that-that... that that's what it was.

320
00:16:35.453 --> 00:16:38.548
- Oh! A jet.
- DON: It's an F-18.

321
00:16:38.623 --> 00:16:40.476
- JOSH: What was that?
- ASHLEY: What did you say. Don?

322
00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.798
- F-18.
- ASHLEY: How do you know?

323
00:16:43.836 --> 00:16:45.383
MARK:
He's got the ear for it.

324
00:16:47.798 --> 00:16:49.401
ASHLEY: All right. I got
as close as I could.

325
00:16:49.425 --> 00:16:52.349
There's this creepy guy
who was just staring me down.

326
00:16:52.428 --> 00:16:54.430
I think he was about
to call security on me.

327
00:16:54.514 --> 00:16:56.200
JOSH:
You actually believe it was the Air Force.

328
00:16:56.224 --> 00:16:57.326
- You believe that...
- I do not.

329
00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.830
- You believe the bearded...
- I don't know what I believe yet!

330
00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:02.192
- I'm open...
- JOSH: The bearded Galileo Society

331
00:17:02.271 --> 00:17:06.117
of Phoenix. Arizona. I'm disappointed.
You're no longer a producer.

332
00:17:06.192 --> 00:17:08.490
ASHLEY:
I am absolutely a producer!

333
00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:24.976
(whispering)
I think I found the section.

334
00:17:26.629 --> 00:17:29.132
JOSH:
"Ancient UFO sightings."

335
00:17:29.215 --> 00:17:31.843
ASHLEY:
Check this out. Petroglyphs.

336
00:17:31.926 --> 00:17:34.975
JOSH:
That's totally a spaceship.

337
00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:37.056
Isn't this that Bible thing
you were talking about?

338
00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:38.391
ASHLEY:
Ezekiel's wheel.

339
00:17:39.892 --> 00:17:41.894
JOSH: Wait. I know
what this reminds me of.

340
00:17:41.978 --> 00:17:43.698
It's like the machine
at the end of Contact.

341
00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:45.026
ASHLEY:
I love that movie.

342
00:17:51.737 --> 00:17:53.785
Okay to go.

343
00:17:53.864 --> 00:17:55.958
(shuddering)
Okay to go-

344
00:17:57.326 --> 00:17:59.203
- JOSH: Initiate drop sequence.
- Okay to go!

345
00:17:59.287 --> 00:18:02.382
Oh. my God. Oh. my God. I think
I'm going through a Wormhole!

346
00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.218
(laughing)

347
00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:09.464
Okay-

348
00:18:13.676 --> 00:18:16.225
JOSH: I don't want
to seem ungrateful for all the help.

349
00:18:16.304 --> 00:18:17.851
but what are we doing here?

350
00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.484
We should be. like.
breaking into Area-51.

351
00:18:24.353 --> 00:18:26.947
ASHLEY: Can you tell us
your name and what you do here?

352
00:18:27.023 --> 00:18:31.119
TONY: My name is Tony Duncan.
I'm from the Apache Nation.

353
00:18:31.193 --> 00:18:33.073
For the most part.
we do a lot of story-telling.

354
00:18:34.113 --> 00:18:36.957
A lot of our stories
of creation talk about

355
00:18:37.033 --> 00:18:39.877
how at one time
we were up in the lights.

356
00:18:39.952 --> 00:18:44.082
up in the sky world. so maybe it was
one of our peoples up there.

357
00:18:44.165 --> 00:18:45.838
ASHLEY:
So. you saw the lights last week?

358
00:18:45.916 --> 00:18:49.261
I didn't see them.
I didn't see them... that exact time.

359
00:18:49.337 --> 00:18:51.840
um. but I just heard
everyone's different stories.

360
00:18:51.922 --> 00:18:55.267
But then eventually. you know.
I seen all the footage of it.

361
00:18:55.343 --> 00:18:57.562
<i>I first thought of the star people.</i>

362
00:18:57.637 --> 00:19:00.686
<i>"That must be them. our relatives."</i>

363
00:19:00.765 --> 00:19:03.018
ASHLEY: You said
you didn't see them that exact time.

364
00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:06.274
- What did you mean?
- Yeah. Actually. um...

365
00:19:06.354 --> 00:19:09.483
way before the lights
that were seen in Phoenix.

366
00:19:09.565 --> 00:19:12.239
my friend that I grew up with...
His name is Pony...

367
00:19:13.611 --> 00:19:16.285
We actually seen some lights
in the same way.

368
00:19:16.364 --> 00:19:18.258
but they were a lot closer.
and we followed them.

369
00:19:18.282 --> 00:19:20.052
- ASHLEY: Wait.
- JOSH: You saw the same formation?

370
00:19:20.076 --> 00:19:22.499
Yeah. yeah. They were in the sky.
and they were actually...

371
00:19:22.578 --> 00:19:24.831
They'd be here and then
they would take off really fast.

372
00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:26.632
and they would move around.

373
00:19:26.707 --> 00:19:29.961
and it was really exciting.
and then it went way out into the field.

374
00:19:30.044 --> 00:19:32.444
Like. we were running way out
into the field for a long time.

375
00:19:32.505 --> 00:19:34.441
- our legs were getting all scratched up.
- (Ashley laughs)

376
00:19:34.465 --> 00:19:37.014
Eventually. it just took off.

377
00:19:37.093 --> 00:19:40.017
Away. high upward. Just...
We couldn't see it anymore.

378
00:19:40.096 --> 00:19:44.351
Uh. but we still talk
about that. Pony and I.

379
00:19:44.433 --> 00:19:48.233
Uh. but that was off over in Salt River.
in the Salt River Reservation.

380
00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.280
ASHLEY:
The bus definitely doesn't go that far.

381
00:19:55.194 --> 00:19:57.413
JOSH:
That's where we're going.

382
00:19:57.488 --> 00:20:00.116
ASHLEY: Well. that's where we're
deciding if we should go.

383
00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:03.078
to be more accurate.

384
00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.289
JOSH: Are you serious?
What. are you scared of sky people?

385
00:20:06.372 --> 00:20:07.965
Of being taken to the spirit world

386
00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.040
- with the Anasazi.
- Well. I kind Of believed him.

387
00:20:12.294 --> 00:20:13.591
JOSH:
Please come.

388
00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.257
I need my producer. you know.

389
00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.557
(laughs)

390
00:20:19.009 --> 00:20:21.478
JOSH: I think it would make
a really sick documentary.

391
00:20:21.554 --> 00:20:23.682
I'll show it to colleges or... somebody.

392
00:20:28.477 --> 00:20:30.445
How do we get there?
(laughs)

393
00:20:32.148 --> 00:20:33.148
(doorbell rings)

394
00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:35.066
JOSH: That's for me.

395
00:20:35.109 --> 00:20:36.656
CAROLINE: Okay. Mark!

396
00:20:36.736 --> 00:20:38.797
- MARK: Mrs. Bishop.
- CAROLINE: I haven't seen you in so long.

397
00:20:38.821 --> 00:20:40.619
- I know. how are you?
- Good. how are you?

398
00:20:40.698 --> 00:20:42.120
<i>Hey.</i>

399
00:20:42.199 --> 00:20:43.371
- You look great.
- Thank you.

400
00:20:43.451 --> 00:20:46.625
- Did you do something with your hair?
- CAROLINE: Oh. Just got it done.

401
00:20:46.704 --> 00:20:48.265
- JOSH: Are you serious?
- Thanks for noticing.

402
00:20:48.289 --> 00:20:50.225
- No problem.
- JOSH: Can you stop flirting with my mom?

403
00:20:50.249 --> 00:20:52.172
I'm not flirting with your mom.

404
00:20:52.251 --> 00:20:53.719
She does look pretty good though.

405
00:20:56.547 --> 00:20:57.890
JOSH: All right. go.

406
00:20:57.965 --> 00:20:59.609
And let's not forget
our most important piece

407
00:20:59.633 --> 00:21:00.930
of equipment on this journey...

408
00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:02.728
(taps)

409
00:21:02.803 --> 00:21:05.352
my 1994 Grand Jeep Cherokee.

410
00:21:05.431 --> 00:21:09.732
Six-cylinder engine.
blood-red finish. roof racks...

411
00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:13.110
16-inch clearance. perfect for maneuvering
over any desert...

412
00:21:13.189 --> 00:21:14.315
(thump)

413
00:21:16.901 --> 00:21:17.948
JOSH: Sorry.

414
00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.632
NEWSREADER <i>(on TV):
phenomenon has returned.</i>

415
00:21:22.656 --> 00:21:24.384
- JOSH: <i>Oh. shit.
- For the second time in one week.</i>

416
00:21:24.408 --> 00:21:26.877
<i>mysterious lights have been spotted
over the Phoenix area...</i>

417
00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:29.796
<i>- Yo.</i> Mark! Look <i>at this!
- This time. over the suburb of Mesa.</i>

418
00:21:29.872 --> 00:21:31.749
<i>The sightings fascinated residents.</i>

419
00:21:31.832 --> 00:21:34.060
MAN <i>(on TV): It was completely silent.
You couldn't hear it.</i>

420
00:21:34.084 --> 00:21:37.338
<i>but you knew it was there.
It was just massive. it was big.</i>

421
00:21:37.421 --> 00:21:40.345
<i>NEWSREADER: Eye-witnesses
describe what they saw as being identical</i>

422
00:21:40.424 --> 00:21:43.111
<i>to the glowing orbs that passed
through the area earlier this week...</i>

423
00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:45.012
Is that them?
Are those your aliens?

424
00:21:45.095 --> 00:21:47.689
A <i>mysterious "V" formation
that flew from west to east.</i>

425
00:21:47.765 --> 00:21:50.410
<i>- The video you're seeing right now...
- JOSH: Dude.</i> I <i>know where this is.</i>

426
00:21:50.434 --> 00:21:52.154
<i>Captured in Mesa
about ten miles from the...</i>

427
00:21:52.978 --> 00:21:56.573
JOSH: Wait. this is it. here on the right.
Right. right. right. right! Go!

428
00:21:56.649 --> 00:21:58.418
- Go. go. go. go. go!
- MARK: Shit. Let me know

429
00:21:58.442 --> 00:22:00.740
- a little earlier next time
- (Josh laughs)

430
00:22:02.488 --> 00:22:03.865
MARK:
Jeez. man.

431
00:22:08.285 --> 00:22:09.286
Dang.

432
00:22:10.538 --> 00:22:11.630
(car doors closing)

433
00:22:13.415 --> 00:22:16.464
JOSH: This is it. This is where
they were. right over that ridge.

434
00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:20.097
MARK: Well...

435
00:22:20.172 --> 00:22:22.015
whatever they were.
they're long gone now.

436
00:22:28.138 --> 00:22:29.310
JOSH:
Dude.

437
00:22:30.766 --> 00:22:31.938
Well. dude. check this out.

438
00:22:34.728 --> 00:22:35.820
Somebody's up there.

439
00:22:38.566 --> 00:22:41.945
You do realize we gotta get up
in. like. six hours. right?

440
00:22:42.027 --> 00:22:43.620
JOSH: Dude.
we're almost to the top.

441
00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.498
MARK:
All right.

442
00:22:48.284 --> 00:22:49.456
Whoa!

443
00:22:49.535 --> 00:22:50.787
Get down.

444
00:22:54.832 --> 00:22:57.802
Dude. kill the light.
What are you doing? Josh?

445
00:22:59.044 --> 00:23:00.044
(switch clicks)

446
00:23:04.633 --> 00:23:06.361
(whispering)
Josh. let's get the hell out of here.

447
00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:07.602
JOSH: Just hang on.

448
00:23:08.679 --> 00:23:10.272
MARK:
Man. those are cops up there.

449
00:23:14.226 --> 00:23:16.149
JOSH:
Dude. there's no plates.

450
