00:34:31.861 --> 00:34:34.239
<i>to those camera equipment
and could check out.</i>

667
00:34:34.322 --> 00:34:38.668
<i>but I don't remember anything
being unaccounted for at the time.</i>

668
00:34:38.743 --> 00:34:41.371
<i>We... we ran that thread out
as far as we could.</i>

669
00:34:41.454 --> 00:34:42.671
and we just couldn't take it.

670
00:34:42.747 --> 00:34:44.827
and law enforcement
couldn't take it anywhere either.

671
00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:51.524
SOPHIE: So that's what the kids would
have been using back in '97. right?

672
00:34:51.548 --> 00:34:53.642
It's a little before my time.

673
00:34:53.717 --> 00:34:56.721
but yeah. probably.

674
00:34:56.803 --> 00:34:59.363
SOPHIE: Do you still have any
of those old cameras laying around?

675
00:34:59.639 --> 00:35:00.731
Yeah.

676
00:35:04.519 --> 00:35:06.942
<i>ASHLEY (on TV):
I'm Ashley Foster. CPTV.</i>

677
00:35:07.022 --> 00:35:09.500
<i>Just want to say hello to all
the new freshmen in the building.</i>

678
00:35:09.524 --> 00:35:10.776
LUISA:
Where did you get this?

679
00:35:10.859 --> 00:35:13.032
SOPHIE:
This was found in Mark Abrams' Jeep

680
00:35:13.111 --> 00:35:16.081
after he went missing
with Ashley and with my brother.

681
00:35:16.156 --> 00:35:18.579
We think Josh had
a second camera with him on the trip.

682
00:35:18.658 --> 00:35:21.411
If he did have one.
it most likely came from the school.

683
00:35:21.494 --> 00:35:24.223
so I was wondering if you thought Ashley
could have checked one out from here.

684
00:35:24.247 --> 00:35:26.170
like. maybe she used
a different name?

685
00:35:26.249 --> 00:35:29.879
It's possible. but like I said.
it was before I started.

686
00:35:29.961 --> 00:35:32.430
Would there have been. like.
a logbook or records of that?

687
00:35:32.505 --> 00:35:34.825
- Like. stuff that might have been...
- It's been 20 years.

688
00:35:35.884 --> 00:35:38.057
I'm so sorry I can't be
of more help to you.

689
00:35:40.805 --> 00:35:44.105
Even if they had a second camera.
it just... it went missing with them.

690
00:35:48.021 --> 00:35:49.694
Just another dead end. you know?

691
00:35:52.942 --> 00:35:54.587
<i>REPORTER (on TV):
And new developments tonight.</i>

692
00:35:54.611 --> 00:35:57.831
<i>Rescuers were forced to call off
their search for three missing teens.</i>

693
00:35:57.906 --> 00:36:01.001
<i>saying there was "no new
credible evidence or clues</i>

694
00:36:01.076 --> 00:36:02.749
<i>to guide the search."</i>

695
00:36:02.827 --> 00:36:04.374
It's like they've been written off.

696
00:36:04.454 --> 00:36:06.432
They've been... my son and his friends
have been abandoned

697
00:36:06.456 --> 00:36:08.333
by the police department.

698
00:36:08.416 --> 00:36:09.977
<i>PIROUZNIA: All the efforts
by law enforcement</i>

699
00:36:10.001 --> 00:36:11.799
<i>to develop some evidence
as to what happened.</i>

700
00:36:11.878 --> 00:36:14.802
they were pretty...
Well. they were negative.

701
00:36:14.881 --> 00:36:17.134
They could never go anywhere
with the case.

702
00:36:18.176 --> 00:36:21.100
I think if they had kids. they'd want
somebody looking for their kid.

703
00:36:29.562 --> 00:36:30.859
(camera clicks)

704
00:36:30.939 --> 00:36:32.566
<i>Dear Ashley.</i>

705
00:36:34.275 --> 00:36:36.277
<i>I know that you're alive...</i>

706
00:36:36.361 --> 00:36:39.410
<i>and that you can hear
my voice right now.</i>

707
00:36:41.241 --> 00:36:45.371
<i>You can't imagine how much your father
and I miss you... and love you.</i>

708
00:36:47.789 --> 00:36:49.791
<i>Every night. I have a dream</i>

709
00:36:49.874 --> 00:36:53.219
<i>that I come downstairs
and you're sitting at the table</i>

710
00:36:53.294 --> 00:36:54.716
<i>like you were never even gone.</i>

711
00:36:56.256 --> 00:36:58.304
<i>I know this means something.</i>

712
00:36:58.383 --> 00:37:02.809
<i>I know it means that you...
are still alive.</i>

713
00:37:04.681 --> 00:37:07.560
<i>(emotionally) Your father and I
will never give up hope.</i>

714
00:37:07.642 --> 00:37:10.737
<i>I love you. Ashley.
Please come home.</i>

715
00:37:17.402 --> 00:37:18.904
<i>MELISSA: I wanted a funeral...</i>

716
00:37:20.947 --> 00:37:23.450
<i>but Jack wouldn't have it.</i>

717
00:37:23.533 --> 00:37:25.706
So. here we are.

718
00:37:28.163 --> 00:37:29.790
The bench was a compromise?

719
00:37:29.873 --> 00:37:31.875
Yep. That's what marriage is about.

720
00:37:50.393 --> 00:37:52.862
It's... uh... Sophie. I don't...

721
00:37:52.937 --> 00:37:54.564
I don't think your brother's alive.

722
00:37:54.647 --> 00:37:56.991
I-I... I don't think...
I don't think he is.

723
00:37:57.066 --> 00:37:58.626
I think something would have developed.

724
00:38:02.739 --> 00:38:04.161
<i>SOPHIE:
Jay. get in here.</i>

725
00:38:06.785 --> 00:38:08.412
- JAY: What's up?
- Have you seen this?

726
00:38:12.040 --> 00:38:15.135
<i>If you'd been here ten years ago
and standing out here and looking up there</i>

727
00:38:15.210 --> 00:38:17.429
<i>at the lights and the view. um.</i>

728
00:38:17.504 --> 00:38:19.482
<i>you would have been astounded.
You would have been amazed.</i>

729
00:38:19.506 --> 00:38:22.680
- JAY: Is that the governor?
- Yeah.

730
00:38:22.759 --> 00:38:25.012
Twenty years ago.
he said the lights were a joke.

731
00:38:25.094 --> 00:38:27.893
He had a whole press conference
making fun of them.

732
00:38:27.972 --> 00:38:29.895
And now he's saying
he saw the lights that night.

733
00:38:29.974 --> 00:38:31.351
<i>MAN (on laptop):
I got four of 'em.</i>

734
00:38:31.434 --> 00:38:33.436
He's basically admitting he lied.

735
00:38:33.520 --> 00:38:36.194
<i>REPORTER: The former governor.
a Vietnam Air Force veteran.</i>

736
00:38:36.272 --> 00:38:39.822
<i>had never publicly
acknowledged seeing it until now</i>

737
00:38:39.901 --> 00:38:41.778
And I suspect that...

738
00:38:41.861 --> 00:38:44.910
unless the Defense Department
proves this otherwise.

739
00:38:44.989 --> 00:38:48.459
that it was probably some form
of an alien spacecraft.

740
00:38:48.535 --> 00:38:52.381
<i>And I think as a public figure. you have
to be very careful about what you say.</i>

741
00:38:52.455 --> 00:38:56.710
<i>because people can have
pretty emotional reactions.</i>

742
00:39:08.721 --> 00:39:09.847
JAY:
Is that him?

743
00:39:14.894 --> 00:39:16.692
Okay. follow me
and just keep rolling.

744
00:39:22.819 --> 00:39:23.820
Excuse me. Mr. Garland?

745
00:39:25.154 --> 00:39:26.841
Hi. I'm Sophie Bishop.
We spoke on the phone.

746
00:39:26.865 --> 00:39:28.538
I'm sorry. I can't help you.

747
00:39:28.616 --> 00:39:30.584
Right. I just have
a couple questions.

748
00:39:30.660 --> 00:39:33.755
You worked for the governor from 1992
until he resigned in '97. is that right?

749
00:39:33.830 --> 00:39:35.958
Sophie. I don't know anything
about your brother.

750
00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:37.476
Okay. what about the Phoenix Lights?

751
00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:39.753
On March 15th. 1997. you went on TV.

752
00:39:39.836 --> 00:39:41.838
and you said that
they were military flares.

753
00:39:41.921 --> 00:39:44.845
Did you see the Governor
on CNN saying that was a lie?

754
00:39:44.924 --> 00:39:46.360
You were his press secretary at the time.

755
00:39:46.384 --> 00:39:48.112
Listen. I really am very sorry
about your brother.

756
00:39:48.136 --> 00:39:49.816
We were just trying not to create a panic.

757
00:39:49.888 --> 00:39:51.435
Who told you to lie?

758
00:39:55.268 --> 00:39:57.191
I mean. what if Josh
was on to something?

759
00:39:58.813 --> 00:40:01.407
We always assumed he got lost
or kidnapped or...

760
00:40:03.610 --> 00:40:05.738
murdered but what if...

761
00:40:07.071 --> 00:40:08.869
JAY:
What if he got abducted by aliens?

762
00:40:10.658 --> 00:40:11.784
(chuckles)

763
00:40:12.702 --> 00:40:14.625
Jesus. I sound like him. don't I?

764
00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:19.384
JAY:
So... now what?

765
00:40:22.211 --> 00:40:23.303
I don't know.

766
00:40:27.008 --> 00:40:28.760
I don't know what
we're doing here anymore.

767
00:40:36.851 --> 00:40:38.203
<i>CAROLINE:
Can't believe you're leaving.</i>

768
00:40:38.227 --> 00:40:39.524
It feels like you just got here.

769
00:40:41.564 --> 00:40:43.362
SOPHIE:
Can I ask you one more question?

770
00:40:46.527 --> 00:40:48.746
Why did you and Dad decide
to call it quits?

771
00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:52.374
Sweetheart.
everyone's divorced now.

772
00:40:52.450 --> 00:40:54.578
I want to know.
Was it Josh's disappearance

773
00:40:54.661 --> 00:40:57.710
or would you guys have
split up anyway?

774
00:41:13.846 --> 00:41:16.850
- ASHLEY (on TV): <i>Hello!</i>
- (Mark chuckles)

775
00:41:16.933 --> 00:41:19.203
MARK: <i>You're going to get
your head taken off by one of those.</i>

776
00:41:19.227 --> 00:41:20.774
<i>ASHLEY:
I want to live here.</i>

777
00:41:20.853 --> 00:41:23.732
<i>- MARK: You want to live here?
- ASHLEY: Yeah. Maybe.</i>

778
00:41:25.316 --> 00:41:26.943
<i>Josh. you want to stop here?</i>

779
00:41:43.626 --> 00:41:45.437
- STEVE: Well. how is she?
- SOPHIE: She's good.

780
00:41:45.461 --> 00:41:48.135
Just getting ready
for the big move. you know.

781
00:41:48.214 --> 00:41:50.693
Well. please tell her. you know.
if she needs any help or anything.

782
00:41:50.717 --> 00:41:52.264
she should call me.

783
00:41:55.596 --> 00:41:57.314
Somebody knows what happened.

784
00:41:59.267 --> 00:42:01.120
JAY: <i>Mark didn't just
wander off into the desert.</i>

785
00:42:01.144 --> 00:42:02.521
<i>He didn't get lost.</i>

786
00:42:02.603 --> 00:42:04.355
That never made sense to me.

787
00:42:09.610 --> 00:42:11.612
<i>SOPHIE:
If Josh hadn't gone missing...</i>

788
00:42:11.696 --> 00:42:13.616
do you think you and Mom
would still be together?

789
00:42:14.323 --> 00:42:15.324
Yeah.

790
00:42:16.617 --> 00:42:17.994
What'd she say?

791
00:42:18.077 --> 00:42:20.277
Sweetheart. what happened was
your brother went missing.

792
00:42:21.164 --> 00:42:22.416
Completely missing.

793
00:42:23.332 --> 00:42:25.084
And it took over our lives.

794
00:42:26.085 --> 00:42:28.525
<i>REPORTER: resources to make sure
these teenagers are found.</i>

795
00:42:34.844 --> 00:42:37.313
If that's true. then what was it.

796
00:42:37.388 --> 00:42:39.061
<i>you know? I don't know.</i>

797
00:42:39.140 --> 00:42:41.518
CAROLINE:
<i>Is Josh dead? Is he alive?</i>

798
00:42:42.435 --> 00:42:43.732
<i>Was he suffering?</i>

799
00:42:43.811 --> 00:42:48.362
Our relationship became about
all those questions.

800
00:42:48.441 --> 00:42:50.081
<i>and your father.
he couldn't do it anymore</i>

801
00:42:50.109 --> 00:42:52.157
and still be the man
that I fell in love with.

802
00:42:52.236 --> 00:42:54.455
and I couldn't do it anymore
and still be his wife.

803
00:42:57.033 --> 00:42:59.286
(jets <i>pass</i> closely overhead)

804
00:42:59.368 --> 00:43:02.372
<i>STEVE: Everybody keeps criticizing me
for. you know. not dealing with it.</i>

805
00:43:02.455 --> 00:43:04.674
I was the only one who was
still out there

806
00:43:04.749 --> 00:43:06.749
trying to figure out
what happened to your brother.

807
00:43:10.213 --> 00:43:13.493
<i>SOPHIE: Do you think there's ever going to
be a point where you can let it go. Dad?</i>

808
00:43:16.761 --> 00:43:18.684
I mean. show... show me his body.

809
00:43:26.521 --> 00:43:28.489
- Good to see you.
- SOPHIE: Love you.

810
00:43:28.564 --> 00:43:30.908
- I love you. too.
- Okay.

811
00:43:30.983 --> 00:43:33.337
All right. Do me a favor:
When you get home. give me a call. okay?

812
00:43:33.361 --> 00:43:34.841
- Okay.
- Let me know you got in okay.

813
00:43:34.904 --> 00:43:36.121
- Yeah.
- Okay.

814
00:43:36.197 --> 00:43:38.592
- We're going to see you Christmas?
- Yeah. I'll see you Christmas.

815
00:43:38.616 --> 00:43:39.833
- Okay.
- Okay.

816
00:43:39.909 --> 00:43:41.136
- All right.
- SOPHIE: Love you.

817
00:43:41.160 --> 00:43:42.412
I love you.

818
00:43:42.495 --> 00:43:43.838
- Bye. Dad.
- Bye.

819
00:44:01.722 --> 00:44:04.159
LUISA <i>(on voicemail):
Hi. Sophie. this is Luisa. Luisa Moreno.</i>

820
00:44:04.183 --> 00:44:06.857
<i>We spoke several months ago
at Canyon Park High.</i>

821
00:44:06.936 --> 00:44:10.816
<i>Um... just call me back when you can.</i>

822
00:44:11.941 --> 00:44:13.363
SOPHIE: Hi.

823
00:44:15.403 --> 00:44:17.371
- Thank you so much for meeting me.
- Yeah.

824
00:44:19.073 --> 00:44:20.551
Did you have a hard time
finding the place?

825
00:44:20.575 --> 00:44:22.202
- No. no. not at all.
- Great.

826
00:44:23.327 --> 00:44:26.547
This place has been on the books
since the late '70s.

827
00:44:26.622 --> 00:44:29.671
Pretty much anything old
or outdated gets thrown in here.

828
00:44:29.750 --> 00:44:31.969
I was throwing away
some garbage over the weekend

829
00:44:32.044 --> 00:44:34.797
and just saw it sitting in the drawer.

830
00:44:34.881 --> 00:44:37.241
Somebody must have thrown it
in here and forgotten about it.

831
00:45:06.412 --> 00:45:08.540
- Can I take this?
- Oh. it's yours.

832
00:45:20.301 --> 00:45:22.554
DAN:
I know you're excited about this. but...

833
00:45:24.597 --> 00:45:26.816
I just don't want you
to get your hopes up. you know?

834
00:45:26.891 --> 00:45:27.892
SOPHIE:
Yeah. I know.

835
00:45:32.230 --> 00:45:33.356
Is that a tape?

836
00:45:34.398 --> 00:45:35.820
- Be careful.
- JAY: I know.

837
00:45:37.944 --> 00:45:39.412
Okay-

838
00:45:39.487 --> 00:45:41.706
- SOPHIE: That's Ashley's handwriting.
- JAY: Really?

839
00:45:51.999 --> 00:45:53.546
Holy shit.

840
00:45:58.839 --> 00:46:00.182
SOPHIE:
Hit play.

841
00:46:02.885 --> 00:46:04.558
I'm going to let you do this.

842
00:46:04.637 --> 00:46:05.934
All right. you ready?

843
00:46:06.847 --> 00:46:08.019
JAY:
Ready.

844
00:46:20.987 --> 00:46:23.866
JAY:
Soph? Sophie?

845
00:47:07.867 --> 00:47:08.867
SOPHIE:
Hi.

846
00:47:10.119 --> 00:47:12.372
Sophie Bishop.
I have an appointment with Captain Groves.

847
00:47:12.455 --> 00:47:13.707
IDs please.

848
00:47:16.500 --> 00:47:18.002
(helicopter approaching)

849
00:47:30.639 --> 00:47:32.562
Just pull over to the side. ma'am.

850
00:47:32.641 --> 00:47:34.143
I need you to wait right over there.

851
00:47:34.226 --> 00:47:36.426
Okay. Is there a problem?
We should have an appointment.

852
00:47:36.479 --> 00:47:38.206
Yes ma'am.
I need you to wait right over there.

853
00:47:38.230 --> 00:47:39.527
Okay-

854
00:47:45.988 --> 00:47:47.490
SOPHIE:
What's it been. like an hour?

855
00:47:57.750 --> 00:47:59.593
That's him.

856
00:47:59.668 --> 00:48:03.639
Okay. uh. just stay here.
keep it low.

857
00:48:03.714 --> 00:48:06.092
(car door alarm beeping)

858
00:48:06.175 --> 00:48:07.722
- Miss Bishop?
- Hi.

859
00:48:08.135 --> 00:48:09.227
Hi there.

860
00:48:14.767 --> 00:48:16.986
So we can do the interview
out here or in your office.

861
00:48:17.061 --> 00:48:18.529
whichever you prefer.

862
00:48:18.604 --> 00:48:19.856
It's not gonna happen.

863
00:48:22.024 --> 00:48:24.447
(speaks indiscernibly)

864
00:48:24.527 --> 00:48:28.031
Okay. but... when we spoke on the phone.
you said that it was fine.

865
00:48:28.114 --> 00:48:31.414
so I <i>guess</i> I'm just wondering what
happened that made you change your mind.

866
00:48:31.492 --> 00:48:33.085
I understand.

867
00:48:33.160 --> 00:48:35.709
- (speaks indiscernibly)
- (helicopter approaching)

868
00:48:35.788 --> 00:48:37.335
Did you watch the footage?

869
00:48:40.459 --> 00:48:42.632
- (helicopter passes overhead)
- (speaks indiscernibly)

870
00:48:48.426 --> 00:48:49.552
Drive safe.

871
00:49:03.691 --> 00:49:04.908
JAY:
You okay?

872
00:49:04.984 --> 00:49:07.282
Yeah. I just honestly
wasn't expecting that.

873
00:49:07.361 --> 00:49:09.784
JAY:
What did he say?

874
00:49:09.864 --> 00:49:12.083
He said. "Don't let that footage get out."

875
00:49:12.700 --> 00:49:13.792
(scoffs)

876
00:49:15.244 --> 00:49:16.712
JAY:
What do you want to do?

877
00:49:21.000 --> 00:49:22.422
What do you think Josh would do?

878
00:49:24.211 --> 00:49:25.929
(static)

879
00:49:32.011 --> 00:49:33.354
JOSH: This is gonna be rad.

880
00:49:35.473 --> 00:49:36.725
Dude.

881
00:49:37.766 --> 00:49:39.985
- MARK: Yeah.
- JOSH: Look at its eye.

882
00:49:40.060 --> 00:49:41.913
- MARK (chuckles): Yeah.
- JOSH: This camera is amazing.

883
00:49:41.937 --> 00:49:44.177
- MARK: Yo. don't get too close.
- JOSH: It smells burnt.

884
00:49:44.231 --> 00:49:46.325
MARK:
It's like males competing for females.

885
00:49:48.194 --> 00:49:49.571
JOSH:
They have the same burns.

886
00:49:49.653 --> 00:49:51.506
Countless stories when UFOs
have been sighted about.

887
00:49:51.530 --> 00:49:53.373
like. animal experimentation.

888
00:49:53.449 --> 00:49:55.247
MARK:
Uh-huh. Yeah. yeah.

889
00:49:55.326 --> 00:49:57.124
They just got cooked by the sun.

890
00:49:58.871 --> 00:50:01.249
- ASHLEY: Woo!
- MARK: Oh shit.

891
00:50:05.044 --> 00:50:06.466
This way.

892
00:50:12.134 --> 00:50:14.196
- MARK: Obviously I'm joking.
- ASHLEY: You just said you look

893
00:50:14.220 --> 00:50:16.314
like older Leo.

894
00:50:16.388 --> 00:50:18.561
<i>People told me that
when Romeo and Juliet came</i> out.

895
00:50:19.767 --> 00:50:20.952
ASHLEY:
What. they said that you...

896
00:50:20.976 --> 00:50:23.604
MARK: That literally made me
more popular in school.

897
00:50:23.687 --> 00:50:25.314
JOSH:
What are you guys talking about?

898
00:50:25.397 --> 00:50:27.820
- What?
- JOSH: What are you guys talking about?

899
00:50:27.900 --> 00:50:29.573
- MARK: You.
- (Ashley laughs)

900
00:50:31.529 --> 00:50:33.873
JOSH:
Just at the top of that ridge.

901
00:50:33.948 --> 00:50:36.292
We wouldn't be able
to see anything from down here.

902
00:50:36.367 --> 00:50:38.386
MARK: Not like we're gonna see
anything up there. either.

903
00:50:38.410 --> 00:50:41.254
JOSH (groans):
Don't be that guy.

904
00:50:42.122 --> 00:50:44.170
We don't need that guy.

905
00:50:44.250 --> 00:50:46.002
You remember where we parked
the car. right?

906
00:50:46.085 --> 00:50:49.259
MARK: Uh... yeah.
It's... that a-way.

907
00:50:50.548 --> 00:50:51.988
- ASHLEY: Ooh. Josh.
- MARK: Oh shit.

908
00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:54.142
Come look at this.

909
00:50:55.052 --> 00:50:56.612
- JOSH: What do you got?
- ASHLEY: Whoa.

910
00:50:57.429 --> 00:50:58.429
Petroglyphs.

911
00:50:59.098 --> 00:51:00.020
JOSH: Oh!

912
00:51:00.099 --> 00:51:02.059
ASHLEY:
Guess this means we're on the right track.

913
00:51:03.018 --> 00:51:04.895
MARK:
Wow. Ancient graffiti.

914
00:51:10.067 --> 00:51:12.536
Now what you see below me
are Native American petroglyphs.

915
00:51:12.611 --> 00:51:15.285
They were probably put here
hundreds of years ago

916
00:51:15.364 --> 00:51:17.833
by the Apache.
They were native to these lands.

917
00:51:17.908 --> 00:51:20.457
very adept at living
in these mountainous regions.

918
00:51:20.536 --> 00:51:22.129
Uh...

919
00:51:22.204 --> 00:51:24.582
the spiral shape
that you see below us...

920
00:51:24.665 --> 00:51:26.977
Historians aren't quite sure
what it could have represented.

921
00:51:27.001 --> 00:51:29.095
It could have represented
ripples in water.

922
00:51:29.169 --> 00:51:30.796
things that they saw in the sky.

923
00:51:32.172 --> 00:51:35.847
And... that's pretty much it.
Petroglyphs.

924
00:51:38.470 --> 00:51:39.767
ASHLEY:
Please be careful.

925
00:51:42.850 --> 00:51:44.022
(yelps)

926
00:51:45.102 --> 00:51:46.102
(laughs)

927
00:51:46.645 --> 00:51:48.113
- You get that?
- JOSH: Yeah.

928
00:51:48.188 --> 00:51:49.690
- It look steep?
- Yeah.

929
00:51:51.942 --> 00:51:53.194
ASHLEY:
You guys are idiots.

930
00:51:59.033 --> 00:52:01.206
ASHLEY: Ah. I should not
have smoked that cigarette.

931
00:52:01.285 --> 00:52:02.582
(imitating gunfire)

932
00:52:07.166 --> 00:52:08.292
ASHLEY:
Whoa.

933
00:52:11.879 --> 00:52:14.348
How far do you want us
to go. Josh?

934
00:52:14.423 --> 00:52:15.970
JOSH:
Just keep going.

935
00:52:38.947 --> 00:52:41.917
ASHLEY: I'm wheezing.
I'm out of breath.

936
00:52:46.789 --> 00:52:48.086
Whoa.

937
00:52:58.008 --> 00:52:59.225
- You rolling?
- JOSH: Yeah.

938
00:52:59.301 --> 00:53:01.224
Check this out.
Oh. shit.

939
00:53:04.139 --> 00:53:05.482
JOSH: Where'd you get those?

940
00:53:05.557 --> 00:53:06.809
Ask Diane Sawyer over there.

941
00:53:06.892 --> 00:53:08.703
ASHLEY: I got it from a guy
at the gas station.

942
00:53:08.727 --> 00:53:10.946
Here. He had a crush on you
or something.

943
00:53:11.021 --> 00:53:12.398
I just used my eyes.

944
00:53:14.024 --> 00:53:16.904
- Yeah. Dude. no. no. Do not film this.
- MARK: We have two more in here.

945
00:53:17.695 --> 00:53:19.163
(Ashley laughing)

946
00:53:31.834 --> 00:53:33.427
is Josh filming this?

947
00:53:33.502 --> 00:53:35.175
- (Ashley laughing)
- Whoa.

948
00:53:35.254 --> 00:53:38.554
Will you please be <i>as</i> careful as possible
with that on a cliff edge.

949
00:53:38.632 --> 00:53:40.555
ASHLEY (laughing):
Sorry.

950
00:53:40.634 --> 00:53:42.978
- Where's Mark?
- He's taking a leak.

951
00:53:43.053 --> 00:53:44.851
Oh. you didn't want to go with him?

952
00:53:44.930 --> 00:53:46.352
Shut up.

953
00:53:49.268 --> 00:53:51.441
- What are you doing?
- It's my turn to interview you.

954
00:53:51.520 --> 00:53:52.706
- This is...
- See how you like it.

955
00:53:52.730 --> 00:53:54.210
It's not a Hitchcock movie. you know.

956
00:53:54.273 --> 00:53:55.900
The director isn't in this one.

957
00:53:57.568 --> 00:53:59.328
MARK: You guys playing
Truth or Dare up here?

958
00:54:00.487 --> 00:54:02.173
- ASHLEY: Want to play Truth or Dare?
- JOSH: Yeah.

959
00:54:02.197 --> 00:54:04.478
- ASHLEY: You go first.
- MARK: You actually want to play?

960
00:54:04.575 --> 00:54:06.175
- ASHLEY: Yeah. why not?
- JOSH: Come on.

961
00:54:06.618 --> 00:54:08.666
- JOSH: I've got a couple beers in me.
- Uh... dare.

962
00:54:09.830 --> 00:54:12.709
ASHLEY: Okay.
I dare you to tell the truth.

963
00:54:14.418 --> 00:54:16.261
That is not how you play the game.

964
00:54:16.336 --> 00:54:18.440
- JOSH: It's fair enough.
- ASHLEY: That is how I play the game.

965
00:54:18.464 --> 00:54:20.967
JOSH: What's. uh... what's the deal
with you and Debbie Gomez?

966
00:54:23.844 --> 00:54:25.437
De-Debbie Gomez?

967
00:54:27.306 --> 00:54:28.353
MARK: Why?

968
00:54:29.767 --> 00:54:31.727
JOSH: Well. the old rumor mill's
been. you know...

969
00:54:32.728 --> 00:54:34.981
We hang out sometimes.
Like. I don't...

970
00:54:35.063 --> 00:54:37.532
JOSH:
You guys play tennis or go golfing?

971
00:54:37.608 --> 00:54:39.986
Why are you being a dick. dude?
Like. we hang out.

972
00:54:40.068 --> 00:54:42.468
- Like. it's not...
- ASHLEY: Why didn't you invite her here?

973
00:54:43.155 --> 00:54:44.883
MARK: I don't know.
I didn't want to make it weird.

974
00:54:44.907 --> 00:54:46.301
JOSH: What do you mean.
"make it weird"?

975
00:54:46.325 --> 00:54:47.326
Why would that be weird?

976
00:54:47.409 --> 00:54:49.137
MARK: I didn't want to make it
like a double date.

977
00:54:49.161 --> 00:54:51.161
- Wait. now that's weird.
- JOSH: Oh. come on. man.

978
00:54:52.122 --> 00:54:54.375
ASHLEY: All right.
we cannot stay here forever.

979
00:54:54.458 --> 00:54:56.256
We need to go as soon
as the sun dips down.

980
00:54:56.335 --> 00:54:58.415
JOSH: Just hold on and enjoy it
for a second. please.

981
00:55:01.381 --> 00:55:03.554
I just want to get this.
It's gorgeous.

982
00:55:09.097 --> 00:55:11.020
- MARK: Josh.
- What?

983
00:55:11.517 --> 00:55:13.144
- MARK: What is that?
- JOSH: What?

984
00:55:13.227 --> 00:55:14.695
- ASHLEY: What?
- MARK: That.

985
00:55:16.647 --> 00:55:18.194
No. no. what is that?

986
00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:21.743
- Ashley.
- ASHLEY: Whoa. what'?

987
00:55:23.403 --> 00:55:26.907
- Wait. Mark. isn't that... what?
- MARK: It's just kind of sitting there.

988
00:55:26.990 --> 00:55:28.927
ASHLEY: Wait.
isn't the Luke Air Force Base over there?

989
00:55:28.951 --> 00:55:30.294
- JOSH: Yeah.
- MARK: Maybe.

990
00:55:30.369 --> 00:55:32.489
JOSH: Probably just something
from the Air Force Base.

991
00:55:33.705 --> 00:55:35.767
- Maybe a helicopter.
- MARK: You're the one looking for UFOs.

992
00:55:35.791 --> 00:55:38.186
- ASHLEY: No. that's not a helicopter.
- MARK: I'm just pointing it out.

993
00:55:38.210 --> 00:55:39.729
ASHLEY:
We'd hear it if it was a helicopter.

994
00:55:39.753 --> 00:55:40.754
JOSH:
Hold on.

995
00:55:43.674 --> 00:55:45.819
- ASHLEY: Wait. Okay. you guys.
- MARK: Think it's a fighter jet?

996
00:55:45.843 --> 00:55:48.363
- MARK: No. that's not a fighter jet.
- ASHLEY: Don't get ahead of yourself.

997
00:55:48.387 --> 00:55:49.434
It's just a light.

998
00:55:49.513 --> 00:55:51.273
MARK: It's not.
You'd hear it. you'd hear it.

999
00:55:53.267 --> 00:55:54.940
ASHLEY:
What? Oh. my God.

1000
00:55:55.018 --> 00:55:57.191
- JOSH: Okay. Okay.
- (explosion)

1001
00:55:57.271 --> 00:55:58.693
- (Ashley gasps)
- MARK: Whoa!

1002
00:56:00.274 --> 00:56:01.992
- MARK: Holy shit!
- What!

1003
00:56:02.901 --> 00:56:04.244
Josh. did you get that?

1004
00:56:04.903 --> 00:56:05.995
JOSH: Hold on.

1005
00:56:06.655 --> 00:56:07.907
MARK: Oh...

1006
00:56:09.533 --> 00:56:11.410
- What was that?
- ASHLEY: I don't...

1007
00:56:11.493 --> 00:56:13.221
- Wait. tell me you got that on camera.
- JOSH: Yes!

1008
00:56:13.245 --> 00:56:14.365
MARK:
Can you play that back?

1009
00:56:16.957 --> 00:56:18.977
- ASHLEY: Oh. my God! Josh.
- MARK: Guys. stop. stop. stop.

1010
00:56:19.001 --> 00:56:20.270
ASHLEY:
Wait. Josh. seriously though.

1011
00:56:20.294 --> 00:56:21.729
JOSH: This is
the greatest day of my life.

1012
00:56:21.753 --> 00:56:23.523
ASHLEY: Oh. my... did you know
that was gonna happen?

1013
00:56:23.547 --> 00:56:24.548
Here. give me that back.

1014
00:56:24.631 --> 00:56:26.192
MARK: Did you know
that was gonna happen?

1015
00:56:26.216 --> 00:56:27.593
Is Luke Air Force Base that way?

1016
00:56:28.719 --> 00:56:30.822
Luke Air Force Base is that way.
but that's not Air Force.

1017
00:56:30.846 --> 00:56:32.657
- MARK: How do you know?
- ASHLEY: You don't know that.

1018
00:56:32.681 --> 00:56:34.524
JOSH:
Because it's not 2150.

1019
00:56:34.600 --> 00:56:36.227
(Mark and Ashley laugh)

1020
00:56:37.227 --> 00:56:38.228
JOSH:
Come back.

1021
00:56:38.312 --> 00:56:39.914
- MARK: All right. man.
- ASHLEY: Twenty minutes.

1022
00:56:39.938 --> 00:56:41.583
MARK: Get like a last pan
or whatever. Let's go.

1023
00:56:41.607 --> 00:56:43.084
Dude. come on.
I'm happy for you. let's go.

1024
00:56:43.108 --> 00:56:45.169
- JOSH: Just ten more minutes?
- MARK: You've done that twice.

1025
00:56:45.193 --> 00:56:46.671
ASHLEY: Do you know
how hard it's gonna be

1026
00:56:46.695 --> 00:56:48.089
to walk through this canyon
in the dark?

1027
00:56:48.113 --> 00:56:49.632
JOSH: I don't see
what the problem is. okay?

1028
00:56:49.656 --> 00:56:51.384
- You know the way back.
- ASHLEY: It's already dark.

1029
00:56:51.408 --> 00:56:52.705
(arguing over each other)

1030
00:56:52.784 --> 00:56:55.179
MARK: The problem is that it starts
to get really dark and really cold.

1031
00:56:55.203 --> 00:56:57.672
and she has a curfew.
and I still have to drive.

1032
00:56:57.748 --> 00:56:59.295
- ASHLEY: Please.
- MARK: Come on.

1033
00:56:59.374 --> 00:57:00.421
Cut. We gotta go.

1034
00:57:00.542 --> 00:57:01.822
ASHLEY:
All right. we're leaving.

1035
00:57:02.794 --> 00:57:04.147
JOSH: What if we get
arrested by. like.

1036
00:57:04.171 --> 00:57:05.468
the Air Force or something?

1037
00:57:05.547 --> 00:57:07.720
MARK: That would actually be
the scariest situation.

1038
00:57:07.799 --> 00:57:10.052
JOSH: Like our parents
don't ever find out.

1039
00:57:10.135 --> 00:57:11.495
like. what's going to happen
to us.

1040
00:57:11.553 --> 00:57:13.396
The Air Force just takes us away
or something.

1041
00:57:14.431 --> 00:57:15.808
MARK: That'd be so sad.

1042
00:57:18.185 --> 00:57:20.622
JOSH: My mom would think I was just
in my room playing with the camera.

1043
00:57:20.646 --> 00:57:22.114
MARK: They wouldn't notice?

1044
00:57:22.189 --> 00:57:24.208
They wouldn't... like. it would take
a couple years I think.

1045
00:57:24.232 --> 00:57:25.700
My parents are noticing right now.

1046
00:57:29.905 --> 00:57:31.122
Oh...

1047
00:57:33.450 --> 00:57:35.498
- (screams)
- You good?

1048
00:57:35.577 --> 00:57:37.124
- Yeah.
- JOSH: Mark.

1049
00:57:37.204 --> 00:57:38.456
- Mark!
- Sorry.

1050
00:57:41.333 --> 00:57:42.810
- ASHLEY: Whoa.
- MARK: Give it to me.

1051
00:57:42.834 --> 00:57:44.677
Give me that.
Give me the UFO.

1052
00:57:45.420 --> 00:57:46.420
- Ah!

1053
00:57:47.506 --> 00:57:49.383
JOSH: After tonight.
you can be producer.

1054
00:57:49.466 --> 00:57:50.934
assistant director.

1055
00:57:52.719 --> 00:57:54.813
You know what?
If you're lucky. we can talk "co."

1056
00:57:54.888 --> 00:57:56.765
- We can what?
- JOSH: We can talk "co."

1057
00:57:56.848 --> 00:57:58.191
- All right.
- JOSH: Co-director.

1058
00:57:58.266 --> 00:58:00.314
MARK:
He's three years older than me.

1059
00:58:00.394 --> 00:58:02.067
JOSH:
His brother voted for Dole.

1060
00:58:02.145 --> 00:58:03.581
- MARK: No. he didn't.
- Bob Dole? Really?

1061
00:58:03.605 --> 00:58:05.208
JOSH:
Yes. he did. Your brother's a moron.

1062
00:58:05.232 --> 00:58:08.432
MARK: My brother's... are you kidding me?
He's an... he's an engineering student.

1063
00:58:09.945 --> 00:58:12.744
He's an engineering student.
He's actually very smart.

1064
00:58:15.117 --> 00:58:16.460
He's gonna be president one day.

1065
00:58:24.292 --> 00:58:27.341
- ASHLEY: Is this a dead end?
- MARK: No. you gotta keep going through.

1066
00:58:27.421 --> 00:58:28.898
ASHLEY:
Are you sure it's not a dead end?

1067
00:58:28.922 --> 00:58:30.984
- MARK: I'm positive it's not a dead end.
- ASHLEY: All right.

1068
00:58:31.008 --> 00:58:32.527
MARK:
We walked through here in the daytime.

1069
00:58:32.551 --> 00:58:34.645
- JOSH: Does it usually get this tight?
- MARK: Yeah.

1070
00:58:38.056 --> 00:58:39.899
We're good.
It goes on for a while.

1071
00:58:39.975 --> 00:58:41.255
I'm gonna be in so much trouble.

1072
00:58:41.309 --> 00:58:43.413
- MARK: You guys need help?
- JOSH: It's worth being in trouble.

1073
00:58:43.437 --> 00:58:44.872
Do you understand what we've seen today?

1074
00:58:44.896 --> 00:58:46.958
Yeah. but I can push it like
an hour. but any longer. it's...

1075
00:58:46.982 --> 00:58:48.950
We would've noticed these
on the way in for sure.

1076
00:58:49.026 --> 00:58:50.699
I don't remember these.

1077
00:58:50.777 --> 00:58:52.779
JOSH: Yeah. I for sure
would have noticed these.

1078
00:58:53.864 --> 00:58:55.104
Mark. are you sure we passed...

1079
00:58:56.783 --> 00:58:57.969
ASHLEY:
Mark where are we going?

1080
00:58:57.993 --> 00:58:59.673
MARK:
Hold on. I'll be super sure. hold on.

1081
00:59:04.124 --> 00:59:05.727
ASHLEY: Are you sure
we're going the right way?

1082
00:59:05.751 --> 00:59:06.751
Yes!

1083
00:59:08.420 --> 00:59:10.263
JOSH:
Why can't you just use the stars. man?

1084
00:59:11.757 --> 00:59:13.259
- Josh.
- MARK: No. it's this way.

1085
00:59:15.135 --> 00:59:16.682
- ASHLEY: Are you positive?
- Yep.

1086
00:59:16.762 --> 00:59:17.762
ASHLEY:
All right.

1087
00:59:19.014 --> 00:59:20.894
- JOSH: Do you guys not hear that?
- BOTH: What?

1088
00:59:25.687 --> 00:59:27.167
- MARK: What?
- ASHLEY: Josh. come on.

1089
00:59:27.773 --> 00:59:30.084
- JOSH: Everything just looks like rocks.
- MARK: I know where we are.

1090
00:59:30.108 --> 00:59:32.253
Yeah. but you keep going
left then right. then left then right.

1091
00:59:32.277 --> 00:59:34.172
You keep complaining
about us being late. so can we go?

1092
00:59:34.196 --> 00:59:35.664
I know exactly where we're going.

1093
00:59:35.739 --> 00:59:37.550
JOSH: I mean. who else
are we gonna listen to anyway?

1094
00:59:37.574 --> 00:59:38.575
(sighs)

1095
00:59:38.658 --> 00:59:40.205
Okay. let's go. What way?

1096
00:59:41.453 --> 00:59:43.296
MARK: Hold on.
Just stop moving. Let me...

1097
00:59:44.539 --> 00:59:45.756
look first.

1098
00:59:52.130 --> 00:59:53.177
(horn blares in distance)

1099
00:59:53.256 --> 00:59:54.508
- (gasps)
- MARK: Well...

1100
00:59:56.635 --> 00:59:58.916
- JOSH: I definitely heard that.
- I just heard something.

1101
01:00:01.932 --> 01:00:03.479
Guys. Get down.

1102
01:00:04.643 --> 01:00:05.860
(whispers)
Get down.

1103
01:00:07.312 --> 01:00:08.655
Mark. get down.

1104
01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:12.821
(horn blares in distance)

1105
01:00:12.901 --> 01:00:14.153
(distant rumbling)

1106
01:00:14.236 --> 01:00:16.276
- ASHLEY: What is that?
- JOSH: It could be a train.

1107
01:00:17.864 --> 01:00:20.583
I-I... I didn't see any tracks out here.

1108
01:00:22.786 --> 01:00:24.834
MARK:
Shh. Just listen.

1109
01:00:26.373 --> 01:00:28.922
(horn blares in distance)

1110
01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:33.046
(distant rumbling)

1111
01:00:43.723 --> 01:00:44.784
MARK:
Okay. we're almost back.

1112
01:00:44.808 --> 01:00:47.128
- ASHLEY: Let's get the hell out of here.
- MARK: Let's go.

1113
01:00:47.811 --> 01:00:50.811
- ASHLEY: Everybody walk faster.
- MARK: Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey. It's okay.

1114
01:00:53.900 --> 01:00:56.254
- Ash. it's all right.
- ASHLEY: We need to get out of here now.

1115
01:00:56.278 --> 01:00:57.951
MARK:
I know. Just calm down.

1116
01:01:00.574 --> 01:01:02.292
Josh...

1117
01:01:02.367 --> 01:01:03.710
do you recognize any of this?

1118
01:01:05.745 --> 01:01:07.181
- Give me the compass.
- Do you want to try'?

1119
01:01:07.205 --> 01:01:08.558
- JOSH: Guys!
- Yes! Give me the compass.

1120
01:01:08.582 --> 01:01:09.629
Get us home.

1121
01:01:09.708 --> 01:01:11.585
- Okay. I will. I will!
- You do it.

1122
01:01:12.460 --> 01:01:13.837
(sighs)

1123
01:01:14.838 --> 01:01:17.933
Okay. so... we came from this way.

1124
01:01:18.758 --> 01:01:20.055
(sighs)

1125
01:01:20.635 --> 01:01:22.387
We got this way.

1126
01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.230
- It's definitely not this way.
- JOSH: Mark?

1127
01:01:25.473 --> 01:01:28.568
- Mark. where you going?
- MARK: Just stay there.

1128
01:01:28.643 --> 01:01:31.289
- JOSH: Mark. where you going?
- I'm gonna find the car from up here!

1129
01:01:31.313 --> 01:01:33.793
JOSH: You're not gonna see anything
up there. it's pitch black.

1130
01:01:37.360 --> 01:01:39.283
ASHLEY: Hey. Josh?
Can you come look at this?

1131
01:01:40.572 --> 01:01:41.698
JOSH:
What?

1132
01:01:42.574 --> 01:01:44.121
ASHLEY:
It's just not working.

1133
01:01:44.201 --> 01:01:46.012
- JOSH: Why would it do that?
- ASHLEY: I don't know.

1134
01:01:46.036 --> 01:01:48.334
- (rumbling)
- Whoa! What is that?

1135
01:01:48.413 --> 01:01:50.882
(rumbling continues)

1136
01:01:50.957 --> 01:01:52.925
ASHLEY: Oh. my God.
What is that?

1137
01:01:53.001 --> 01:01:55.504
(panting)

1138
01:01:55.587 --> 01:01:57.190
- Josh. I don't like this.
- JOSH: Hold on. wait.

1139
01:01:57.214 --> 01:01:59.808
Just stay still.
Where is it coming from?

1140
01:01:59.883 --> 01:02:01.055
ASHLEY: I don't know.

1141
01:02:01.801 --> 01:02:02.973
- Oh!
- JOSH: Ashley.

1142
01:02:03.053 --> 01:02:04.475
Oh. my God.

1143
01:02:04.554 --> 01:02:06.272
(humming)

1144
01:02:07.432 --> 01:02:08.524
JOSH:
Oh. my God.

1145
01:02:08.600 --> 01:02:10.602
(rumbling)

1146
01:02:11.853 --> 01:02:12.945
Josh.

1147
01:02:15.857 --> 01:02:17.734
(Ashley screaming)

1148
01:02:17.817 --> 01:02:20.070
JOSH: Ashley. run! Run!

1149
01:02:20.654 --> 01:02:22.873
(static)

1150
01:02:22.948 --> 01:02:24.040
JOSH:
Oh. my God!

1151
01:02:25.617 --> 01:02:27.585
- Get down! Get down!
- ASHLEY: Ow!

1152
01:02:28.370 --> 01:02:29.371
JOSH:
Run!

1153
01:02:30.664 --> 01:02:32.257
(Ashley continues screaming)

1154
01:02:34.751 --> 01:02:35.968
(wind gusting)

1155
01:02:40.131 --> 01:02:42.975
JOSH:
Jesus Christ! Whoa.

1156
01:02:43.051 --> 01:02:46.305
Holy shit. Oh. my God.

1157
01:02:48.348 --> 01:02:49.975
ASHLEY:
Oh. my God.

1158
01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:55.776
(breathes shakily)

1159
01:02:55.855 --> 01:02:57.482
Josh? Josh?

1160
01:02:58.775 --> 01:03:00.402
- Are you okay?
- JOSH: Yeah. you?

1161
01:03:01.069 --> 01:03:02.069
Yeah.

1162
01:03:03.154 --> 01:03:04.497
JOSH:
Your hands are shaking.

1163
01:03:05.657 --> 01:03:06.954
I'm scared.

1164
01:03:07.033 --> 01:03:09.377
- JOSH: What was that?
- I don't know.

1165
01:03:10.829 --> 01:03:12.877
- (rustling)
- (Ashley gasps)

1166
01:03:12.956 --> 01:03:14.833
Oh. Mark! Are you all right?

1167
01:03:17.043 --> 01:03:18.590
JOSH:
Mark. tell me you saw that. man.

1168
01:03:19.504 --> 01:03:21.097
I saw the car.

1169
01:03:21.172 --> 01:03:22.775
- You saw the what?
- I saw the car. It's close.

1170
01:03:22.799 --> 01:03:23.846
JOSH:
You saw the car?

1171
01:03:23.925 --> 01:03:26.045
- ASHLEY: What are you talking about?
- MARK: Come on.

1172
01:03:28.138 --> 01:03:30.032
- ASHLEY: Mark. where are you going?
- MARK: I don't know.

1173
01:03:30.056 --> 01:03:31.826
MARK: Can we just get
the hell out of here. please?

1174
01:03:31.850 --> 01:03:33.397
- ASHLEY: No. wait!
- JOSH: Mark!

1175
01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:34.898
- Mark!
- MARK: Let's go!

1176
01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.275
ASHLEY:
Okay. Mark. slow down!

1177
01:03:36.354 --> 01:03:37.957
- JOSH: Tell me you saw that. man.
- ASHLEY: Hey.

1178
01:03:37.981 --> 01:03:39.709
MARK: Can we just get
the hell out of here. please?

1179
01:03:39.733 --> 01:03:41.502
ASHLEY: I think we should have
a group huddle first.

1180
01:03:41.526 --> 01:03:42.527
JOSH:
Mark. what was that?

1181
01:03:43.486 --> 01:03:44.588
Come on. man. what did you see?

1182
01:03:44.612 --> 01:03:46.507
Josh. I need you to stop talking
until we find the car.

1183
01:03:46.531 --> 01:03:48.134
ASHLEY: Okay. You're sure
the car's over here?

1184
01:03:48.158 --> 01:03:49.760
MARK:
Yes. I'm positive the car's over here.

1185
01:03:49.784 --> 01:03:52.412
JOSH (laughing): Can we please
talk about what we got on tape?

1186
01:03:52.495 --> 01:03:53.621
ASHLEY:
Oh yes!

1187
01:03:53.705 --> 01:03:55.378
- MARK: I told you.
- ASHLEY: The car!

1188
01:03:55.457 --> 01:03:57.084
Oh. Oh!

1189
01:03:57.917 --> 01:04:02.172
(panting)

1190
01:04:02.255 --> 01:04:03.507
ASHLEY:
Thank God.

1191
01:04:07.761 --> 01:04:09.855
MARK:
We're not gonna see anything. Josh.

1192
01:04:09.929 --> 01:04:11.351
(Josh chuckling)

1193
01:04:12.474 --> 01:04:13.743
MARK:
Josh. get your ass in the car.

1194
01:04:13.767 --> 01:04:15.202
JOSH: Ah. come on.
what if they come back?

1195
01:04:15.226 --> 01:04:16.786
I swear to God
I'll leave you. Let's go.

1196
01:04:16.853 --> 01:04:19.134
- JOSH: Just five minutes. man.
- Come on. Get in the car.

1197
01:04:22.275 --> 01:04:24.503
- (exhales deeply)
- ASHLEY: You really didn't see anything?

1198
01:04:24.527 --> 01:04:26.655
I thought I did.
I thought I saw these. um...

1199
01:04:26.738 --> 01:04:30.242
- JOSH: Like circles?
- No. dumbass. Like rings.

1200
01:04:30.325 --> 01:04:31.969
And they were above me.
and then they were gone.

1201
01:04:31.993 --> 01:04:33.415
Wait. rings like the petroglyphs?

1202
01:04:34.871 --> 01:04:36.214
Did you guys not see these?

1203
01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:41.586
All right. it was obviously
in my head. all right? Let's just go.

1204
01:04:41.669 --> 01:04:44.388
- (console beeping)
- (engine sputtering)

1205
01:04:44.464 --> 01:04:46.182
(long beep)

1206
01:04:46.257 --> 01:04:48.601
ASHLEY:
Oh shit. Oh shit.

1207
01:04:48.676 --> 01:04:50.804
- (engine starts)
- JOSH: There we go.

1208
01:04:50.887 --> 01:04:52.184
ASHLEY:
Oh. thank God.

1209
01:04:54.182 --> 01:04:57.152
You guys. what the hell
just happened to us?

1210
01:04:57.227 --> 01:04:59.605
JOSH: No one has ever filmed
anything like that before.

1211
01:05:00.647 --> 01:05:01.739
Let's just get out of here.

1212
01:05:03.149 --> 01:05:05.868
- (pop music playing on radio)
- MARK: Signs of civilization.

1213
01:05:05.944 --> 01:05:09.494
ASHLEY: I know.
It feels so nice to listen to music.

1214
01:05:10.240 --> 01:05:11.800
MARK:
You're gonna be real famous. Josh.

1215
01:05:11.825 --> 01:05:13.427
- ASHLEY: I think he will be.
- JOSH: Thank you.

1216
01:05:13.451 --> 01:05:15.249
MARK:
Yeah. until they think it's all faked.

1217
01:05:15.328 --> 01:05:18.628
(pop music plays on radio)

1218
01:05:23.461 --> 01:05:25.304
- Are you okay. Mark?
- MARK: Yeah.

1219
01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:28.557
- ASHLEY: Are you sure?
- Yeah. I'm fine.

1220
01:05:28.633 --> 01:05:30.635
ASHLEY:
Your head feels a little bit hot.

1221
01:05:30.718 --> 01:05:32.891
Yeah. I have a stomachache.
but I'm good.

1222
01:05:34.013 --> 01:05:35.811
(static on radio)

1223
01:05:35.890 --> 01:05:37.493
JOSH: I think Mark's gonna be
the most famous

1224
01:05:37.517 --> 01:05:39.315
when people see
how bad he pissed his pants.

1225
01:05:39.394 --> 01:05:41.497
- (Ashley laughing)
- MARK: Dude. shut up. Are you serious?

1226
01:05:41.521 --> 01:05:43.916
- ASHLEY: Mark. you were really scared.
- MARK: I would have loved to see

1227
01:05:43.940 --> 01:05:46.877
- either of you up there by yourselves.
- ASHLEY: You should have seen your face.

1228
01:05:46.901 --> 01:05:48.244
Okay-

1229
01:05:48.319 --> 01:05:49.821
(static on radio)

1230
01:05:49.904 --> 01:05:51.156
JOSH:
What's up with the radio?

1231
01:05:51.239 --> 01:05:53.037
(static continues)

1232
01:05:57.954 --> 01:06:00.391
- I have to drive for two hours.
- JOSH: All right. all right. all right.

1233
01:06:00.415 --> 01:06:01.917
MARK:
And we're done shooting.

1234
01:06:04.461 --> 01:06:06.259
Whoa. whoa. what is that?

1235
01:06:06.337 --> 01:06:08.556
- MARK: What?
- ASHLEY: Is that a car?

1236
01:06:08.631 --> 01:06:11.009
- What is that?
- MARK: What the hell is that?

1237
01:06:12.343 --> 01:06:13.435
JOSH:
It's just a car.

1238
01:06:13.511 --> 01:06:15.030
ASHLEY: No. no. no.
there's no way on earth.

1239
01:06:15.054 --> 01:06:17.102
MARK: Josh. cars don't have
one light. What is that?

1240
01:06:17.182 --> 01:06:18.729
Is it getting clo... turn that off.

1241
01:06:18.808 --> 01:06:20.105
ASHLEY: Sorry.

1242
01:06:20.185 --> 01:06:22.329
- Okay. Mark. speed up. Go. go. go. go. go.
- MARK: I am.

1243
01:06:22.353 --> 01:06:24.457
- (engine revving)
- MARK: Josh. is it getting closer?

1244
01:06:24.481 --> 01:06:26.361
ASHLEY:
Yeah. it's getting closer. I can see it.

1245
01:06:27.775 --> 01:06:29.211
- Oh. my God.
- MARK: What the hell is that?

1246
01:06:29.235 --> 01:06:30.713
Josh. it's not a car!
Josh. it's not a car!

1247
01:06:30.737 --> 01:06:32.423
MARK:
Josh. what's it doing? What's it doing?

1248
01:06:32.447 --> 01:06:35.087
- Is it getting closer?
- ASHLEY: Oh. my God. it's right behind us!

1249
01:06:35.283 --> 01:06:36.830
Mark. speed up!
Go. go. go. go. go!

1250
01:06:36.910 --> 01:06:38.378
MARK:
I'm going as fast as I can!

1251
01:06:38.453 --> 01:06:39.750
(all scream)

1252
01:06:41.122 --> 01:06:42.999
- JOSH: Don't stop. dude!
- My car just died!

1253
01:06:43.082 --> 01:06:45.311
- ASHLEY: Oh. my God. I don't like this!
- MARK: What just happened?

1254
01:06:45.335 --> 01:06:47.053
What just happened?
The car isn't going.

1255
01:06:47.128 --> 01:06:49.023
The car isn't going.
What the hell just happened?

1256
01:06:49.047 --> 01:06:50.149
ASHLEY (whispering):
Josh.Josh.

1257
01:06:50.173 --> 01:06:51.893
- MARK: What the heck!
- ASHLEY: Okay. stop.

1258
01:07:00.391 --> 01:07:03.941
Uh. everything was fine with the car.
and now... it's not.

1259
01:07:04.020 --> 01:07:05.522
The engine doesn't have power.

1260
01:07:05.605 --> 01:07:07.528
The whole car in general
doesn't have power.

1261
01:07:10.485 --> 01:07:11.828
(Spits) Ah.

1262
01:07:12.946 --> 01:07:14.323
My mouth tastes weird.

1263
01:07:15.198 --> 01:07:18.668
JOSH: Adrenaline.
It's why your mouth tastes weird.

1264
01:07:18.743 --> 01:07:19.960
(beer can pops)

1265
01:07:21.704 --> 01:07:23.126
No water.

1266
01:07:26.960 --> 01:07:28.462
Yo. Josh. come help me.

1267
01:07:28.545 --> 01:07:29.762
JOSH: Cool.

1268
01:07:30.838 --> 01:07:32.840
MARK:
Ash. put the E-brake up.

1269
01:07:34.551 --> 01:07:37.851
There we go. You ready?
Let's go.

1270
01:07:40.598 --> 01:07:42.896
(both grunting)

1271
01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:44.569
JOSH:
What the hell is going on. man?

1272
01:07:44.644 --> 01:07:46.021
MARK:
I don't know. man.

1273
01:07:47.272 --> 01:07:48.615
All right. that's good. Ash.

1274
01:07:55.613 --> 01:07:57.411
- JOSH: Mark?
- Yeah?

1275
01:07:58.408 --> 01:07:59.568
JOSH:
Hey. man. you all right?

1276
01:08:01.452 --> 01:08:03.625
- Yeah.
- JOSH: Dude. Dude. your nose is bleeding.

1277
01:08:03.705 --> 01:08:04.752
ASHLEY:
What's going on?

1278
01:08:06.708 --> 01:08:09.052
- What happened?
- I just have a nose bleed.

1279
01:08:10.128 --> 01:08:11.345
- ASHLEY: What?
- I'm fine.

1280
01:08:11.421 --> 01:08:12.468
- JOSH: You okay?
- Yeah.

1281
01:08:12.547 --> 01:08:14.608
I used to get 'em all the time
when I was a kid. Stop.

1282
01:08:14.632 --> 01:08:16.475
- JOSH: Oh. my God.
- It is the dry air.

1283
01:08:16.551 --> 01:08:18.224
- You're sweating.
- I'm fine.

1284
01:08:19.846 --> 01:08:20.938
- Is it any better?
- Oh.

1285
01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:23.475
Here.

1286
01:08:25.393 --> 01:08:27.020
How far do you think
the gas station is?

1287
01:08:28.062 --> 01:08:30.611
- Mark?
- Uh. seven. eight miles.

1288
01:08:31.357 --> 01:08:32.404
JOSH:
In the dark?

1289
01:08:33.151 --> 01:08:35.504
We should stay with the car.
we're not doing that. That's crazy.

1290
01:08:35.528 --> 01:08:37.951
Yeah. we are. No. honest.
it'll take a couple hours.

1291
01:08:38.031 --> 01:08:39.453
it'll be open.
we'll get some help.

1292
01:08:39.532 --> 01:08:41.955
- Let's go. Josh?
- Come on.

1293
01:08:42.702 --> 01:08:44.542
- JOSH: Ashley. this is crazy.
- (Ashley sighs)

1294
01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:49.750
JOSH:
Shoot.

1295
01:08:54.631 --> 01:08:56.178
- JOSH: You all right?
- Huh?

1296
01:08:56.799 --> 01:08:58.016
You cool?

1297
01:08:58.092 --> 01:08:59.320
- You all right?
- ASHLEY: Hey. guys.

1298
01:08:59.344 --> 01:09:00.584
- JOSH: Yeah.
- ASHLEY: Come on.

1299
01:09:05.516 --> 01:09:06.859
(Winces)

1300
01:09:09.270 --> 01:09:11.898
(shuddering)

1301
01:09:11.981 --> 01:09:13.233
You guys. it's getting cold.

1302
01:09:23.910 --> 01:09:25.036
JOSH:
Hey. Ash?

1303
01:09:26.371 --> 01:09:28.999
Hey. Ash?
Let's let Mark catch up.

1304
01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:34.170
Something's wrong with him. Josh.

1305
01:09:34.253 --> 01:09:37.223
- JOSH: It's. uh. just a nose bleed.
- No.

1306
01:09:37.298 --> 01:09:38.971
It's not just a nose bleed.

1307
01:09:40.385 --> 01:09:43.559
I mean. something happened
to him up there.

1308
01:09:43.638 --> 01:09:46.687
It's not just a coincidence. the car dying
right when the lights came back.

1309
01:09:49.852 --> 01:09:52.526
JOSH: So what are you saying?
They're messing with us?

1310
01:09:55.358 --> 01:09:57.326
They're following us.

1311
01:09:57.402 --> 01:09:58.403
MARK: Guys!

1312
01:10:03.032 --> 01:10:04.033
Do you hear that?

1313
01:10:06.411 --> 01:10:08.709
- Did you hear that?
- ASHLEY: Hear what?

1314
01:10:09.747 --> 01:10:10.919
Come here.

1315
01:10:12.125 --> 01:10:13.468
ASHLEY: Mark. come on.

1316
01:10:15.712 --> 01:10:17.055
MARK:
No. someone's out there.

1317
01:10:21.092 --> 01:10:22.389
(shouting) Hey!

1318
01:10:22.468 --> 01:10:25.187
- ASHLEY: Mark!
- MARK: Come... come here! Come help us!

1319
01:10:25.263 --> 01:10:26.731
ASHLEY:
Dude. come on!

1320
01:10:28.725 --> 01:10:30.443
MARK:
Come help us!

1321
01:10:30.518 --> 01:10:32.579
- What is he talking about?
- MARK: Dan. I can hear you.

1322
01:10:32.603 --> 01:10:33.479
- JOSH: Mark!
- ASHLEY: Mark!

1323
01:10:33.563 --> 01:10:34.610
Shh.

1324
01:10:35.982 --> 01:10:38.485
Dan! Thank God!

1325
01:10:38.568 --> 01:10:40.796
- ASHLEY: What? Do you hear anything?
- MARK: Guys. it's my brother!

1326
01:10:40.820 --> 01:10:42.242
How did you find us?

1327
01:10:42.321 --> 01:10:43.841
ASHLEY:
What the hell is he talking about?

1328
01:10:43.865 --> 01:10:46.163
- JOSH: Mark! Come on!
- ASHLEY: Mark!

1329
01:10:46.242 --> 01:10:47.710
JOSH! Mark. come on!

1330
01:10:48.703 --> 01:10:50.000
(rumbling)

1331
01:10:50.079 --> 01:10:51.752
JOSH:
Whoa! Jesus! Ashley!

1332
01:10:51.831 --> 01:10:52.923
ASHLEY: Mark!

1333
01:10:52.999 --> 01:10:54.967
(wind gusting)

1334
01:11:01.716 --> 01:11:02.943
ASHLEY (whispering):
What was that?

1335
01:11:02.967 --> 01:11:04.059
JOSH: I don't know.

1336
01:11:09.807 --> 01:11:12.526
OW! Ah! Ah!

1337
01:11:19.066 --> 01:11:22.616
(panting)

1338
01:11:36.751 --> 01:11:39.300
- Mark!
- JOSH: Mark! What the hell?

1339
01:11:41.589 --> 01:11:42.841
Mark!

1340
01:11:46.093 --> 01:11:48.937
ASHLEY: Hey. Mark!
I can't see his headlamp.

1341
01:11:50.556 --> 01:11:51.556
JOSH:
Mark?

1342
01:11:54.185 --> 01:11:55.357
Come on. man.

1343
01:12:00.900 --> 01:12:01.901
Hold on.

1344
01:12:02.777 --> 01:12:03.653
(clicks)

1345
01:12:03.736 --> 01:12:06.615
- Did you hear anything?
- ASHLEY: No.

1346
01:12:06.697 --> 01:12:08.175
JOSH: 'Cause Mark said
he heard voices.

1347
01:12:08.199 --> 01:12:10.199
ASHLEY: What voices. Josh?
There's no one out here.

1348
01:12:10.827 --> 01:12:13.330
Let's just find Mark.
Hey. Mark!

1349
01:12:13.412 --> 01:12:15.210
JOSH:
He looked so sick. Mark?

1350
01:12:15.289 --> 01:12:16.757
How much further
could he have gone?

1351
01:12:16.833 --> 01:12:19.006
- JOSH: I don't... I don't know.
- ASHLEY: Mark!

1352
01:12:20.169 --> 01:12:21.170
Mark!

1353
01:12:23.005 --> 01:12:24.678
JOSH:
Oh. God.

1354
01:12:24.757 --> 01:12:26.851
ASHLEY: We're not going anywhere
until we find Mark.

1355
01:12:26.926 --> 01:12:28.018
Mark!

1356
01:12:28.094 --> 01:12:29.774
- JOSH: Ashley.
- No. we're gonna find him.

1357
01:12:29.804 --> 01:12:30.976
JOSH:
Ashley.

1358
01:12:31.055 --> 01:12:32.807
ASHLEY:
Mark!

1359
01:12:33.516 --> 01:12:34.813
Mark!

1360
01:12:34.892 --> 01:12:37.691
- (sobbing) He's gone.
- He's not gone.

1361
01:12:37.770 --> 01:12:40.023
He's not gone.
He's just...

1362
01:12:40.106 --> 01:12:43.986
He's just lost.
He's just lost. okay?

1363
01:12:44.068 --> 01:12:46.036
What are you talking about?

1364
01:12:46.112 --> 01:12:47.864
He was there.
and then he was gone.

1365
01:12:47.947 --> 01:12:50.791
Something took him.
They took him.

1366
01:12:50.867 --> 01:12:52.710
No. No one took him.

1367
01:12:52.785 --> 01:12:55.459
He's probably behind
one of these hills. Okay?

1368
01:12:55.538 --> 01:12:59.133
- But we... we've gotta keep moving.
- (continues sobbing)

1369
01:12:59.208 --> 01:13:01.757
We've gotta keep moving.
we've gotta find people.

1370
01:13:01.836 --> 01:13:04.259
We can come back and help Mark. all right?
So come on.

1371
01:13:05.882 --> 01:13:08.226
Come on. Please.

1372
01:13:10.511 --> 01:13:12.559
- Okay.
- All right. all right.

1373
01:13:13.306 --> 01:13:14.398
Okay-

1374
01:13:17.143 --> 01:13:20.773
All right. I'm okay. I'm okay.

1375
01:13:23.482 --> 01:13:25.610
JOSH: Listen...

1376
01:13:25.693 --> 01:13:28.822
don't worry about him anyway.
Okay? He's been in...

1377
01:13:28.905 --> 01:13:33.001
the Boy Scouts
since he was like two years old.

1378
01:13:33.075 --> 01:13:35.123
- ASHLEY: Mark!
- JOSH: And he's go...

1379
01:13:36.245 --> 01:13:37.713
Holy shit!

1380
01:13:37.788 --> 01:13:40.587
- What? What is it?
- Look! Look. it's a light!

1381
01:13:42.251 --> 01:13:44.504
- ASHLEY: Is it them?
- JOSH: No!

1382
01:13:44.587 --> 01:13:47.431
That's like... like a street light
or a trailer or something.

1383
01:13:49.592 --> 01:13:50.684
I told you.

1384
01:13:51.928 --> 01:13:54.226
Okay. Let's go.

1385
01:13:56.390 --> 01:13:58.813
JOSH:
We can get some water. Call for help.

1386
01:14:02.647 --> 01:14:04.365
ASHLEY:
Let's go. Yeah.

1387
01:14:08.694 --> 01:14:11.072
- ASHLEY: Are you still filming?
- Yeah.

1388
01:14:12.156 --> 01:14:15.160
I'm trying to film landmarks
so we can retrace our steps.

1389
01:14:16.118 --> 01:14:17.118
ASHLEY:
That's smart.

1390
01:14:19.622 --> 01:14:21.215
I think I just need
a second to rest.

1391
01:14:23.751 --> 01:14:25.094
We're gonna be okay.

1392
01:14:25.169 --> 01:14:26.887
We're gonna find him. Josh.

1393
01:14:26.963 --> 01:14:28.180
JOSH: Yeah.

1394
01:14:33.135 --> 01:14:34.387
(Josh coughs)

1395
01:14:38.391 --> 01:14:39.483
- ASHLEY: Shit!
- What?

1396
01:14:40.851 --> 01:14:43.104
ASHLEY: Damn it!
I just dropped my flashlight.

1397
01:14:43.187 --> 01:14:44.860
JOSH:
Okay. where is it?

1398
01:14:44.939 --> 01:14:46.816
No. there's no way
we can get it. Look down.

1399
01:14:47.566 --> 01:14:49.239
Shit!

1400
01:14:49.318 --> 01:14:51.741
JOSH: Okay. we're gonna
use this as a flashlight.

1401
01:14:53.864 --> 01:14:55.664
Okay. just flash it
in front of me. all right.

1402
01:14:55.700 --> 01:14:57.247
- ASHLEY: Okay.
- JOSH: Don't drop it.

1403
01:14:57.326 --> 01:14:58.553
- ASHLEY: All right.
- Okay. let's go.

1404
01:14:58.577 --> 01:15:01.831
ASHLEY: Whoa.
How long does this battery last?

1405
01:15:01.914 --> 01:15:03.507
JOSH:
About an hour.

1406
01:15:03.582 --> 01:15:04.959
ASHLEY:
Oh. shit.

1407
01:15:07.003 --> 01:15:08.050
JOSH:
Is it bright enough?

1408
01:15:08.713 --> 01:15:10.590
ASHLEY:
Yeah. it's okay.

1409
01:15:11.799 --> 01:15:13.346
JOSH:
We're almost down.

1410
01:15:15.469 --> 01:15:17.597
ASHLEY (gasps):
Josh?

1411
01:15:17.680 --> 01:15:18.897
JOSH:
What?

1412
01:15:20.182 --> 01:15:21.809
God. Oh. my God.

1413
01:15:23.310 --> 01:15:25.529
(shivering)
I have t... I have tissues.

1414
01:15:25.604 --> 01:15:27.948
Get 'em. Where's... where's...

1415
01:15:28.024 --> 01:15:30.064
- It's in my front pocket.
- JOSH: The front pocket?

1416
01:15:32.153 --> 01:15:34.497
Here. Here. Here.

1417
01:15:35.322 --> 01:15:36.494
Okay-

1418
01:15:38.242 --> 01:15:40.162
JOSH: I shouldn't have brought
you guys out here.

1419
01:15:41.746 --> 01:15:44.795
It's not your fault.
I wanted to come.

1420
01:15:45.541 --> 01:15:46.541
Why?

1421
01:15:47.626 --> 01:15:48.923
I don't know.

1422
01:15:52.131 --> 01:15:53.731
I just wanted to do something different.

1423
01:15:54.842 --> 01:15:56.059
Something unexpected.

1424
01:15:59.555 --> 01:16:01.978
Something my dad
wouldn't expect. anyway.

1425
01:16:04.894 --> 01:16:05.941
I'm good.

1426
01:16:06.437 --> 01:16:07.797
- JOSH: You sure?
- Yeah. I'm good.

1427
01:16:08.981 --> 01:16:10.198
I'm good. Come on.

1428
01:16:15.654 --> 01:16:16.997
(Ashley coughing)

1429
01:16:23.537 --> 01:16:24.663
(thump)

1430
01:16:24.747 --> 01:16:27.170
JOSH:
Shit. Ashley?

1431
01:16:28.209 --> 01:16:31.679
(coyotes howling. screeching)

1432
01:16:31.754 --> 01:16:33.097
ASHLEY: Shit.

1433
01:16:38.094 --> 01:16:39.437
Let's go.

1434
01:16:40.221 --> 01:16:41.221
JOSH: Okay.

1435
01:16:41.263 --> 01:16:42.355
(flies buzzing)

1436
01:16:46.727 --> 01:16:48.274
JOSH:
Oh. God.

1437
01:16:50.731 --> 01:16:52.654
- Josh.
- Hey.

1438
01:16:52.733 --> 01:16:54.076
Hey. we can't go back.

1439
01:16:56.320 --> 01:16:58.118
Come on.
Just don't look at 'em.

1440
01:17:01.492 --> 01:17:02.994
- Shit.
- ASHLEY: They're burned.

1441
01:17:04.411 --> 01:17:05.708
They burned them.

1442
01:17:18.050 --> 01:17:19.267
ASHLEY: Ah!

1443
01:17:23.347 --> 01:17:24.439
Ashley?

1444
01:17:27.143 --> 01:17:28.144
Josh?

1445
01:17:28.853 --> 01:17:31.652
- JOSH: It's okay. It's okay. It's okay.
- (Ashley crying)

1446
01:17:31.730 --> 01:17:32.731
JOSH:
It's okay.

1447
01:17:41.031 --> 01:17:43.329
- ASHLEY: Do you hear that?
- JOSH: Hear what?

1448
01:17:46.328 --> 01:17:47.329
ASHLEY:
Do you hear that?

1449
01:17:54.753 --> 01:17:55.754
JOSH:
Ashley?

1450
01:17:58.507 --> 01:17:59.508
Ashley?

1451
01:18:01.010 --> 01:18:02.307
You don't hear that?

1452
01:18:08.767 --> 01:18:09.768
JOSH:
Ashley?

1453
01:18:10.352 --> 01:18:12.104
- ASHLEY: It's my dad.
- JOSH: Ashley?

1454
01:18:12.188 --> 01:18:13.235
- (rumbling)
- JOSH: Oh!

1455
01:18:13.314 --> 01:18:15.533
- It's my dad! (laughing)
- JOSH: Oh. my... Oh. my God!

1456
01:18:16.317 --> 01:18:18.536
- Ashley!
- ASHLEY: Dad!

1457
01:18:19.612 --> 01:18:21.785
- Dad!
- JOSH: Oh!

1458
01:18:23.032 --> 01:18:25.080
ASHLEY:
I'm right here!

1459
01:18:25.159 --> 01:18:27.912
- JOSH: Ashley. stop!
- Dad. I'm here!

1460
01:18:29.538 --> 01:18:31.586
I'm right here!

1461
01:18:32.082 --> 01:18:34.756
- Dad. I'm here!
- JOSH: Ashley. don't!

1462
01:18:35.502 --> 01:18:36.719
(explosion)

1463
01:18:36.795 --> 01:18:39.469
It's my dad!
(laughing) It's my dad!

1464
01:18:40.674 --> 01:18:42.051
(laughing) Dad!

1465
01:18:44.511 --> 01:18:45.558
(wind gusting)

1466
01:18:45.638 --> 01:18:47.481
<i>Ashley. stop!</i>

1467
01:18:48.515 --> 01:18:49.892
Dad!

1468
01:18:50.601 --> 01:18:53.275
(static)

1469
01:18:55.898 --> 01:18:57.571
(Josh panting)

1470
01:18:58.943 --> 01:19:00.490
(rumbling)

1471
01:19:04.323 --> 01:19:05.620
Hello!

1472
01:19:11.538 --> 01:19:13.290
(panting continues)

1473
01:19:14.541 --> 01:19:15.713
(groans)

1474
01:19:16.585 --> 01:19:18.553
(glass shatters)

1475
01:19:19.630 --> 01:19:23.225
(screaming)

1476
01:19:29.723 --> 01:19:31.020
(screaming continues)

1477
01:19:31.100 --> 01:19:35.731
(explosions)

1478
01:19:42.987 --> 01:19:45.240
(screaming continues)

1479
01:19:49.410 --> 01:19:50.878
(static)

1480
01:19:54.290 --> 01:19:56.213
(wind blowing)

1481
01:20:12.766 --> 01:20:15.645
(birds chirping)

1482
01:20:48.010 --> 01:20:51.810
(ominous music playing)

1483
01:22:24.565 --> 01:22:26.909
(classical score playing)

1484
01:23:47.231 --> 01:23:50.952
(ominous music playing)
